    "summary": "Glen Helen’s early‑morning set dazzles with a blazing Playin’ → Shakedown and crisp China/Rider.",
    "review": "What unfolds at Glen Helen Regional Park on September 5, 1982 is the kind of high‑octane festival opener that still makes you grin when the tape rolls. The band bursts out of the gates with a thunderous Playing In The Band → Shakedown Street intro that sets a relentless pace for the early‑morning crowd. From there they ride straight into a smoking China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider, and a gritty New Minglewood Blues where Bob’s slide shines. The second set keeps the momentum with a tight Space → Not Fade Away stretch and a solid run through Truckin' into the classic drum/space sequence, before winding down with Sugar Magnolia, U.S. Blues and a raucous Satisfaction encore. Across all available tapes the performance feels locked‑in, with Garcia’s leads cutting cleanly, Lesh anchoring the jams, and Brent’s keyboards threading color through the rapid tempo changes, even if a few mixes catch his piano a bit over‑mic’d.",
